module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Module.FinitePresentation
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Spectrum.Prime.Module
import Sheaf.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.CauchyBinet
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Adjugate

/-!
# The support of a finitely presented module

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 051B, lemma-support-finite-presentation-constructible
(blueprint: lem-pur-finitely-presented-support-complement).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v

namespace Module

/-- The support of a finitely presented module is closed with quasi-compact complement.
Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 051B
(blueprint: lem-pur-finitely-presented-support-complement).

Proof: choose a finite presentation `B^u → B^v → M → 0` with matrix `A` and
surjection `q`. The elements `q(e_j)` generate `M`. Let `I` be generated by the finitely
many maximal minors `d_S` of `A`. For `v = 0`, the empty minor is one and `M = 0`.
If the localization at a prime `p` vanishes, choose annihilators outside `p` for the
finitely many generators and multiply them to obtain `s` outside `p`. Exactness gives
a matrix `C` with `AC = s • 1`. Cauchy--Binet (lem-weil-pbc-cauchy-binet) gives
`s^v = ∑ S, d_S * det(C_S) ∈ I`, so `I` is not contained in `p`.
Conversely, a minor `d_S` outside `p` and the adjugate identity
(lem-weil-pbc-matrix-adjugate-identity) give `A E_S adj(A^S) = d_S • 1`.
Applying `q` shows that `d_S` annihilates every generator, hence all of `M`.
The fraction equality for localization then gives `M_p = 0`. Thus the support is
`V(I)`, closed in the Zariski topology (def-weil-affine-spectrum).
Each basic open `D(f)` is homeomorphic to the spectrum of the localization away from `f`
(lem-weil-pbc-spec-localization-away-basic-open), hence quasi-compact by spectrum
compactness (lem-weil-pbc-spec-basic-opens-unit-ideal-quasi-compact).
The complement of `V(I)` is the finite union of the `D(d_S)`. Restrict any open cover
to each such basic open, choose a finite subcover, and combine these finite choices.
When there are no minors the union is empty; when `v = 0` it is `D(1)`. -/
theorem isClosed_support_and_isCompact_compl
    (B : Type u) (M : Type v) [CommRing B] [AddCommGroup M] [Module B M]
    [Module.FinitePresentation B M] :
    IsClosed (Module.support B M) ∧ IsCompact (Module.support B M)ᶜ := by
  sorry

end Module
